IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`
IMPORT `cp3-retirement-pension`

-- Tests of cp3-retirement-pension.l4 (sections 45 and 46). Expected values are worked by hand from the text.

§ `Tests -- section 45`

#ASSERT `s 45(1) — the basic amount of a benefit` 500 EQUALS 500
-- one step: 1000 x 105 / 100 = 1050
#ASSERT `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment` 1000 105 100 EQUALS JUST 1050
-- no change in the index: the same amount
#ASSERT `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment` 1000 100 100 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- the earlier index is zero: not covered
#ASSERT `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment` 1000 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- two steps: 1000 x 103 / 100 = 1030, then 1030 x 106.09 / 103 = 1060.9
#ASSERT `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in a later year after the annual adjustments` 1000 (LIST 100, 103, 106.09) EQUALS JUST 1060.9
-- the year it became payable: no adjustment
#ASSERT `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in a later year after the annual adjustments` 1000 (LIST 100) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- no index at all: not covered
#ASSERT `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in a later year after the annual adjustments` 1000 EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- an index of zero in the middle: the step after it meets a zero earlier index: not covered
#ASSERT `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in a later year after the annual adjustments` 1000 (LIST 100, 0, 50) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 46(1)`

-- 25% of 4000 = 1000; 8.33% of 1000 = 83.3; 33.33% of 500 = 166.65: 1249.95
#ASSERT `s 46(1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension` 4000 1000 500 EQUALS 1249.95
-- only the average monthly pensionable earnings: a quarter
#ASSERT `s 46(1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension` 4000 0 0 EQUALS 1000
-- only the first additional: 8.33% of 1200 = 99.96
#ASSERT `s 46(1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension` 0 1200 0 EQUALS 99.96
-- only the second additional: 33.33% of 300 = 99.99
#ASSERT `s 46(1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension` 0 0 300 EQUALS 99.99

§ `Tests -- section 46(2)`

-- a weighted average: (1000 x 24 + 800 x 360) / (24 + 360) = 312000 / 384 = 812.5
#ASSERT `s 46(2) — the portion of a retirement pension under paragraph (1)(a) for a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces` TRUE TRUE 1000 800 24 360 EQUALS JUST 812.5
-- the division does not reduce the pension: the subsection does not apply
#ASSERT `s 46(2) — the portion of a retirement pension under paragraph (1)(a) for a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces` TRUE FALSE 1000 800 24 360 EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a former disability pension recipient
#ASSERT `s 46(2) — the portion of a retirement pension under paragraph (1)(a) for a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces` FALSE TRUE 1000 800 24 360 EQUALS NOTHING
-- no months at all: not covered
#ASSERT `s 46(2) — the portion of a retirement pension under paragraph (1)(a) for a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces` TRUE TRUE 1000 800 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- the interval of subsections (3) and (7)`

-- born 15 June 1960: 65 on 15 June 2025, deemed 1 July 2025. Commencing January 2018: 90 months before, taken as 60.
#ASSERT `cp3 — the time interval between the commencement of a retirement pension and the month of reaching 65, in months, at most five years` (YearMonthDay 2018 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS 60
-- commencing July 2024: 12 months before
#ASSERT `cp3 — the time interval between the commencement of a retirement pension and the month of reaching 65, in months, at most five years` (YearMonthDay 2024 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS 12
-- commencing July 2026: 12 months after
#ASSERT `cp3 — the time interval between the commencement of a retirement pension and the month of reaching 65, in months, at most five years` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS 12
-- commencing in the month of reaching 65: no interval
#ASSERT `cp3 — the time interval between the commencement of a retirement pension and the month of reaching 65, in months, at most five years` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS 0
-- exactly five years after: 60
#ASSERT `cp3 — the time interval between the commencement of a retirement pension and the month of reaching 65, in months, at most five years` (YearMonthDay 2030 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS 60

§ `Tests -- section 46(3)`

-- Arguments: the basic monthly amount, the month the pension commences, the date of birth, the Minister's factor.
-- born 15 June 1940: 65 on 15 June 2005, deemed 1 July 2005. A pension commencing January 2005: 1000 x 0.97 = 970
#ASSERT `s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1940 6 15) 0.97 EQUALS JUST 970
-- commencing with the month of reaching 65 (July 2005): not "a month other than" it
#ASSERT `s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2005 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1940 6 15) 0.97 EQUALS NOTHING
-- December 1986 is not after December 31, 1986... it is before January 1987
#ASSERT `s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` 1000 (YearMonthDay 1986 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) 0.97 EQUALS NOTHING
-- January 1987: the first month
#ASSERT `s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` 1000 (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) 0.97 EQUALS JUST 970
-- December 2010: the last month
#ASSERT `s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2010 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1945 6 15) 1.03 EQUALS JUST 1030
-- January 2011: subsection (3.1)'s case, not this one
#ASSERT `s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1945 6 15) 1.03 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 46(3.1)`

-- born 15 June 1950: 65 on 15 June 2015, deemed 1 July 2015. A pension commencing January 2011: 1000 x 0.965 = 965
#ASSERT `s 46(3.1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010, adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7)` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) 0.965 EQUALS JUST 965
-- commencing June 2015, the month before the month of reaching 65: applies
#ASSERT `s 46(3.1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010, adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7)` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) 0.995 EQUALS JUST 995
-- commencing July 2015, the month of reaching 65: no factor
#ASSERT `s 46(3.1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010, adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7)` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- December 2010: before the subsection
#ASSERT `s 46(3.1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010, adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7)` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2010 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1945 6 15) 0.97 EQUALS NOTHING
-- after 65: an upward factor
#ASSERT `s 46(3.1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010, adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7)` 1000 (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) 1.0684 EQUALS JUST 1068.4

§ `Tests -- section 46(4)`

-- F1 = 0.7, P1 = 1000, F2 = 0.8 (less than 1), P2 = 1200: (0.7 x 1000 + 0.8 x 200) / 1200 = 860 / 1200 = 43 / 60
#ASSERT `s 46(4) — the adjustment factor applied after a division increases a retirement pension` 0.7 1000 0.8 1200 EQUALS JUST (43 DIVIDED BY 60)
-- F2 would be 1.2: the lesser of that and 1 is 1: (700 + 200) / 1200 = 0.75
#ASSERT `s 46(4) — the adjustment factor applied after a division increases a retirement pension` 0.7 1000 1.2 1200 EQUALS JUST 0.75
-- P2 zero: not covered
#ASSERT `s 46(4) — the adjustment factor applied after a division increases a retirement pension` 0.7 1000 0.8 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 46(5)`

-- Arguments: an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise, retirement and reduced survivor's pension, the basic monthly amount, the downward factor, the reduction, the index of the commencement year, the index of the year of reduction.
-- X = 100 x 100 / 110 = 1000 / 11; the factor applies to 1000 - X: (1000 - X) x 0.8 + X = 800 + 0.2 X = 9000 / 11
#ASSERT `s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` FALSE TRUE 1000 0.8 100 100 110 EQUALS JUST (9000 DIVIDED BY 11)
-- an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise: the subsection does not apply
#ASSERT `s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` TRUE TRUE 1000 0.8 100 100 110 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the survivor's pension is not reduced under subsection 58(2)
#ASSERT `s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` FALSE FALSE 1000 0.8 100 100 110 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the factor is an upward one: only a downward factor is dealt with
#ASSERT `s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` FALSE TRUE 1000 1.1 100 100 110 EQUALS NOTHING
-- a factor of exactly 1 is not a downward one
#ASSERT `s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` FALSE TRUE 1000 1 100 100 110 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the index of the year of the reduction is zero: not covered
#ASSERT `s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` FALSE TRUE 1000 0.8 100 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 46(6)`

-- born 15 June 1950: 65 deemed 1 July 2015. A division on 10 March 2016, a pension commencing September 2017: 18 months from March 2016
#ASSERT `s 46(6) — the time interval, in months, on which the upward adjustment factor for an increase due to a division after age 65 is based` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2016 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2017 9 1) EQUALS JUST 18
-- a division before the age is deemed reached: not covered by the subsection
#ASSERT `s 46(6) — the time interval, in months, on which the upward adjustment factor for an increase due to a division after age 65 is based` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2017 9 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the division on the day the age is deemed reached: after reaching it
#ASSERT `s 46(6) — the time interval, in months, on which the upward adjustment factor for an increase due to a division after age 65 is based` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2017 9 1) EQUALS JUST 26
-- a division in the month the pension commences: not "before" the commencement
#ASSERT `s 46(6) — the time interval, in months, on which the upward adjustment factor for an increase due to a division after age 65 is based` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2017 9 20) (YearMonthDay 2017 9 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- more than five years between: five years
#ASSERT `s 46(6) — the time interval, in months, on which the upward adjustment factor for an increase due to a division after age 65 is based` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2016 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2023 1 1) EQUALS JUST 60
